comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T11:24:02.403Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: excluding closed items inside precedents makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"real SDK upsert\" test/core.test.ts fail on a terminal refusal/fix precedent. Restored byte-for-byte; the complete SDK reader includes all statuses."
  "2026-10-13T19:26:17.644Z",codex-agent,"PR 1 finding 1 accepted: parse optional repo and PR precedent filters independently, retaining validation for provided values and strict coordinates for import, round and verdict. Add real-tracker dispatch regression and function-only revert proof."
  "2026-10-13T19:33:04.551Z",codex-agent,"Accepted findings have passing real-tracker regressions. Reverting only the relevant dispatch, classification, import or apply function makes each targeted test fail on the original behavior; fixed functions restored. See docs/pr-1-review-round.md for per-finding evidence and packed dogfood UX."
  "2026-10-13T19:39:01.231Z",codex-agent,"Fix round complete: isolated npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 91/91 tests, 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across 17 sources, zero duplication, production audit, pack, changelog, release attestation and packed npm/native Bun acceptance. All five latest function-only revert proofs fail as expected; fixed functions restored. Packed dogfood re-import created zero duplicates, preserves five explicit fix verdicts, repairs notice and legacy major classifications, and supports repo-only precedent search. Identity gate and added-line privacy checks report zero. See docs/pr-1-review-round.md. Live review actions were not applied."
